Z||000007||FieroGT||08-30-99||03:25 PM||||The results are in on my 2 Fieros:<p>'85 SE-V6 - 160-180 miles to tank, car has <br>154,000 miles (rebuilt motor @ 97,000) and still truckin'.<p>'86 GT - 210-240 miles to tank, last week got 268! 120,000 miles, took headgaskets @ 118,000. <p>All of this is roundtown miles with occasonal 4-5 mile highway blasts. Both cars have 4-speeds, are shifted around 3,000 RPM, with the occasional blast to 5,000 RPM. I drive both cars the same and cannot explain the fuel mileage difference. Theories, please?
Z||000008||mrfiero||08-31-99||10:55 PM||||I had an '87 coupe that went 423 miles/tank<br>on a trip to Texas earlier this year... I <br>got about 36 MPG and filled up with 11.6 <br>gallons (almost empty).  I could go at least <br>300 miles/tank around town with mixed highway driving.<p>I can go between 300-350 miles/tank in <br>my '88 Formula 5-sp. (highway miles--275-300 <br>mixed city/hwy). I even went as far as 385 miles/tank on my recent trip to Columbus<br>for the national show (I was driving on <br>fumes!).<p>I suppose it really depends on what year <br>Fiero you have (later years have bigger gas<br>tanks), what transmission you have (5-sp. <br>get better mileage), how well  maintained <br>your Fiero is and how you drive your Fiero <br>as to how far you can go on a tank of gas.<p><br>The worst mileage I ever got was on an '88 <br>GT auto......I only got 130 miles out of a <br>tank once.  It was all stop & go city <br>driving.....I think it factored out to 12 <br>MPG.  Yuck!<p>
